      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The routine employment and wide indications for ascending phlebography for evaluating the deep and superficial systems prior to specific therapy makes it desirable that the patient should feel as little pain as possible. By using suitable measures before and after the examination, optimal position of the patient and appropriate choice of instruments, as well as local anaesthesia with a Dermo-Jet pressure injector, it is possible to render the examination almost completely painless."},
